{"name":"King Kong","hex":"#161410","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"King Kong","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A fictional giant ape, the eponymous star of several movies.","A king (playing card)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/King_Kong"}],"entries":[{"title":"King Kong","blocks":[{"text":"King Kong, also referred to simply as Kong, is a fictional monster, a giant gorilla who has appeared in various media since 1933. The character has become an international pop culture icon, appearing in several movies, comics, videogames and television shows. His first appearance was in the novelization of the 1933 film King Kong from RKO Pictures, with the film premiering a little over two months later."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/King_Kong_1933_Promotional_Image.png/330px-King_Kong_1933_Promotional_Image.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Kong","wikidata":"Q216810"},{"title":"King Kong (2005 film)","blocks":[{"text":"King Kong is a 2005 epic monster film directed, co-written, and produced by Peter Jackson. It is the ninth entry in the King Kong franchise and the second remake of the 1933 film of the same title, the first being the 1976 remake. The film stars Naomi Watts, Jack Black, Adrien Brody, Thomas Kretschmann, Colin Hanks, Jamie Bell, and Andy Serkis as the motion-capture performer of Kong. Set in 1933, it follows the story of an ambitious and unscrupulous filmmaker who tricks his cast and hired ship crew into travelling to mysterious Skull Island. There they encounter various prehistoric creatures and a legendary giant gorilla known as Kong, whom they capture and take to New York City to exhibit."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Kingkong_bigfinal1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Kong_(2005_film)","wikidata":"Q160215"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/King_Kong_ESB.JPG/500px-King_Kong_ESB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/King_Kong_ESB.JPG/1280px-King_Kong_ESB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/King_Kong_ESB.JPG/500px-King_Kong_ESB.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"King Kong graphics at the Empire State Building","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKing_Kong_ESB.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Cooper-Kong.jpg/500px-Cooper-Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Cooper-Kong.jpg/500px-Cooper-Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Merian C. Cooper glances up at his creation.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACooper-Kong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia